cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Register and character in the Legacy of Kain series: annotation
  and analysis code
message: >-
  If you use this annotation or code, please cite both the software
  and the associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guzsvinecz
    given-names: Tibor
    name-particle: Dr
    affiliation: >-
      University of Pannonia, Faculty of Information Technology,
      Veszprém, Hungary
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3273-313X"
    email: guzsvinecz.tibor@zek.uni-pannon.hu
repository-code: "https://github.com/zyzyx02/LoKDuality"
abstract: >-
  Stand-off register annotation for the five Legacy of Kain games
  (1996 to 2003), covering 1,768 speech blocks and 39,247 words,
  together with the Python corpus-construction pipeline and the R
  analysis code. Each block is labelled as narration or dialogue,
  and the provenance of every label is recorded. The dialogue text
  is not redistributed; a rebuild script reconstructs the corpus
  from a user's own copies of the source transcripts.
keywords:
  - register variation
  - character voice
  - narration
  - video game dialogue
  - corpus annotation
  - emotion lexicon
  - Legacy of Kain
license: MIT
